commit f59d5aee2db7f7bad58157e5518ac2af00e2c434
Author: Jacob Boerema <jgboerema@gmail.com>
Date:   Fri Aug 14 13:03:57 2026 -0400

    tools/xml2po: fix #692 Differentiate between Shift and Shift key
    
    When used as a single word translatable sentence. The <keycap> tags
    were removed from the translatable sentence.
    This makes it impossible to differentiate between the word Shift used
    alone and the key with the same name, which may need different
    translations.
    
    To handle this, we need special handling for <keycap> tags in xml2p
    both for:
    - Creating pot files, in which case we need to add <keycap> around
    keys that are used without further text.
    - Creating the merged xml files, in which case we need to make sure
    we don't add doucle <keycap> tags around keys.
    
    These changes will necessarily cause some new translations to be
    required as well as some fuzzy ones.

